58-concept of δ-sequence (see Page 7).
59-(1) (Section 3) Given a polynomial f ∈ K[x, y], decide if f has one place at infinity and if
60-yes, compute the set of its approximate roots and the generators of its semigroup. Our
61-approach here is the irreducibility criterion given by S.S. Abhyankar in [4]. This criterion is
62:straightforward from the equation. It is based on the notion of generalized Newton polygons
63-and it does not use neither the resolution of singularities nor the calculation of Puiseux series
64-at infinity. We have implemented this procedure using the numericalsgps ([9]) GAP ([11])
65-package, and named it SemigroupOfValuesOfPlaneCurveWithSinglePlaceAtInfinity.
66:(2) (Section 4) Given a sequence of integers in N, decide if this sequence generates the semigroup
67-of a polynomial at infinity, and if it is the case, calculate an equation of such a polynomial.
68:Our equation allows in particular, using the notion of generalized Newton polygons, the
69-calculation of all polynomials with the given semigroup. The GAP function implemented for
70-this is CurveAssociatedToDeltaSequence (compare with [10, Algorithm 1]).
71-(3) (Section 5) Given a positive integer g, compute the set of semigroups of polynomials with
72:one place at infinity with genus g (hence with conductor 2g). Note that if Γ is such a
73-semigroup and if f is a polynomial with one place at infinity whose semigroup is Γ, then g
74-is the geometric genus of a nonsingular element of the pencil (f − λ)λ∈K , and 2g is the rank
75-of the K-vector space K[x, y]/(fx , fy ), where fx (respectively fy ) denotes the x-derivative
76:(respectively the y-derivative) of f . The function DeltaSequencesWithFrobeniusNumber
77-has been designed to do this. In [10] there is an alternative procedure to compute all
78-δ-sequences with given genus.
79-All these GAP functions will be included in the next release of the package numericalsgps.
