7-Abstract. We study possible configurations of singular points occuring on general algebraic
8-curves in CP 2 via Floer theory. To achieve this, we describe a general formula for the H1 -action
9:on the knot Floer complex of the knotification of a link in S 3 , in terms of natural actions on
10:the link Floer complex of the original link. This result may be of interest on its own.
11-
12-1. Introduction
13-1.1. General context. Let C be a complex curve in CP 2 . The curve C is called rational, if
14-C is irreducible and there exists a continuous degree one map from S 2 to C. The curve C is
15:called cuspidal, if all its singularities have one branch (i.e. their links have one component). The
16:problem of classifying rational cuspidal curves was posed in the 19th century and has not been
17-fully resolved ever since, despite significant recent progress. For instance, Palka and Pelka gave
18-a partial classification (in fact, a full classification under a so-called rigidity conjecture) [45, 46],
19-and Koras and Palka [44, 26] solved a century old conjecture of Coolidge–Nagata [8, 33] related
20:to cuspidal curves.
21-In [13], Fernandez de Bobadilla, Luengo, Melle-Hernandez and Némethi indicated a connection
22:between Seiberg–Witten invariants and rational cuspidal curves. As a consequence of these
23-connections, they stated a conjecture binding coefficients of Alexander polynomials of singular
24:points of a rational cuspidal curve. This conjecture was proved in [5]; we refer to [2] for a precise
25-connection of the results of [5] and the conjecture of [13]. The methods of [5] used the relation
26:of semigroups of singular points with Vs -invariants of knots together with the Ozsváth–Szabó
27-d-invariant inequality.
28-The methods of [5] were later generalized by Bodnár, Borodzik, Celoria, Golla, Hedden and
29:Livingston [1, 4] to the case of non-rational cuspidal curves. Further generalization required
30:better understanding of Heegaard Floer theory of multi-component links of singularities. The
31-techniques used in the present paper build on recent developments in the Heegaard Floer TQFT
32-due to the third author as well as many others; see [20, 22, 51, 52, 55, 54].
