171-Our last application concerns complex algebraic curves all of whose singular points are of
172:type Am , that is, singular points whose links are T p2, m ` 1q torus knots/links. Such curves
173-are extensively studied in the literature; see for instance the survey [30]. We give a bound for
174-the maximal n such that an algebraic curve of the degree d has an A2n singularity, as well as a
175:bound on the number of cusps of an algebraic curve of degree d with nodes and ordinary cusps,
176-see Section 7. While these bounds are not the best found in the literature, they are the first
177-bounds using Floer theories. There is a chance that these bounds could be refined by using
178-other versions of Floer homology.
