216:cuspidal curves of higher genus in Subsections 6.3 and 6.5.
217:In Section 7 we consider curves whose only singularities are T p2, kq torus knots or links. The
218-main results are Theorem 7.2, and Theorem 7.4. Theorem 7.2 concerns curves which have only
219:double points and ordinary cusps. Theorem 7.4 bounds the maximal index n such that a curve
220-of degree d can have an A2n singularity. The main algebraic tool is Proposition 7.6, which allows
221-us to turn the obstructions from the previous sections into a closed formula.
