225-Definition 1.3. A singular curve in the smooth category in CP 2 is a smooth map ι : Σ Ñ CP 2 ,
226-which is a diffeomorphism onto its image except for finitely many points. The surface Σ is a
227-smooth, closed, two-dimensional manifold. The image C “ ιpΣq is a smooth submanifold except
228-possibly at points z1 , . . . , zN . For each such point zi , there exists a ball Bi Ă CP 2 with center
229:zi , such that C is transverse to BBi and C X Bi is a cone over Ki “ BBi X C.
230:The genus of a singular curve is the genus of Σ. The set Ki is a link in BBi . It is called a link
231-of singularity.
232:Algebraic curves have one more restriction. The link of a singularity of an algebraic curve is
233:an algebraic link (see [10]). For example, every algebraic knot is a sufficiently positive iterated
234-torus knot.
235:Definition 1.4. A singular curve in the smooth category is of algebraic type if all links of its
236:singularities are algebraic links. A singular curve in the smooth category is of weakly algebraic
237:type if all links of its singularities are either algebraic links or their mirrors.
238-In the present paper, unless specified otherwise, one can always replace a term “algebraic
239-curve” by a “singular curve in the smooth category of weakly algebraic type”. We refer to [14]
240-for a related construction.
