+`Forum of Mathematics, Sigma, 2 (2014)` and DOI `10.1017/fms.2014.28`,
+not JEMS. The BHL and BLZ venue data in the charged report also match the
+arXiv metadata.
+
+The three OPEN items are not equally scoped.
+
+`affine_singularity_records` is a real row-level absence: the conductor-12
+census supplies `Delta_aff=6` and the infinity delta-sequence, not a
+partition of affine singularities for every curve in the row. For the
+specific associated curve, though, this review supplies the record:
+one affine multibranch point at the origin, three smooth branches, pairwise
+intersection multiplicities `2,2,2`, local delta `6`.
+
+`lemma_multibranch_HF` is the decisive candidate-level absence. The
+associated curve has a three-branch common-tangent affine germ, outside BL
+2014, BHL 2017, and BLZ 2024 Theorem 6.4. No replacement theorem was found
